# Don't run dependency install scripts.
#
# The only packages here that have one are:
#  - better-sqlite3: ships prebuilt binaries for linux/macOS/windows (x64, arm64,
#    musl) and sets "gypfile": false, but npm drops that flag from
#    package-lock.json and runs an implicit `node-gyp rebuild` anyway. That step
#    builds nothing when a prebuild exists, yet it downloads Node headers from
#    nodejs.org first, so `npm ci` fails on machines without internet access.
#  - esbuild (via tsx, drizzle-kit): its postinstall only relinks the platform
#    binary that is already installed as an optional dependency.
# Skipping them also keeps third-party code from running at install time.
#
# On a platform without a better-sqlite3 prebuild, compile it once with:
#   npm rebuild better-sqlite3 --ignore-scripts=false
ignore-scripts=true
